# Bentley Continental GT third generation, 2018-2024.
#
# The 2018 car: the aluminium-intensive body with the wider matrix grille,
# the crystal-cut headlamps and the 6.0 W12. UK showrooms from May 2018;
# replaced in 2024.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bentley_Continental_GT
#
# Dimensions 4.850 x 1.954 x 1.405 m, wheelbase 2.851 m, with 2.187 m over
# the mirrors (Bentley's own third-generation specification sheet).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level profile of a UK car, EX19 YKZ.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the 17 standard colours of Bentley's UK brochure "The
# New Continental GT" of June 2018. Weights 20, 16, 12, 10, total 58,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 333 km/h. Comfort 160/570, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 160. Classes 3,4.
# Dates: intro May 2018; retires staggered 2032-2035 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bentley-continental-gt-3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bentley-continental-gt-3.dae. References:
# citycars/references/bentley-continental-gt-3/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the W12 coupe is modelled. The rear haunch crease is
# softer than in the photograph, and the crystal optics and brightwork are
# simplified. The mirror span is 2.187 m.


obj=citycar
